---
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// HOMEPAGE LABORATORY — VERSION A: "Editorial Trailhead"  (design experiment, 2026-08-25)
//
// THE HYPOTHESIS UNDER TEST. One dominant attraction, plus a few much smaller glimpses of other
// terrain. Its job: *there is a lot of unusual intellectual terrain here — start somewhere
// interesting.* Compare against /lab/exhibit, which tests the opposite bet.
//
// NOT the homepage, NOT linked from navigation, excluded from the sitemap. Production untouched.
//
// v2 CHANGES (Huayin, 2026-08-25):
//  · THE LEAD IS SEMANTICALLY REPAIRED. The first cut said three ratios were equally legitimate
//    answers. Two of them were not answers at all. See the long note above READINGS.
//  · The Intelligence dialogue is CUT. With the synthesis gone its payoff went with it, and a fourth
//    small object after the lead was starting to smell like the grid this composition exists to
//    avoid. A's range claim now rests on three genuinely different KINDS of object — a data puzzle,
//    a philosophical joke, and a working machine — rather than on covering three topics.
//  · The publication shelf is CUT. A homepage does not need a research section; it needs sources
//    where they are earned. The serious source now sits directly under the attraction that provokes
//    it, and the Research door in the nav carries anyone who wants the library.
//  · The explicit "you were in three different places" synthesis is CUT, down to one light line that
//    names no architecture. Cornerstone revelations should accumulate until a reader finds the rhyme
//    themselves.
//  · The "what is worth seeing today" dateline is CUT. That phrasing promised an editorial cadence
//    nobody has committed to; a standing exhibit that changes when something better earns the spot
//    is the honest posture, and the wording should not quietly sign us up to a content treadmill.
//
// NO-JS. Everything works with JavaScript off; the lead is `<input type=radio>` + `:checked ~`. This
// page ships zero JavaScript of its own.
//
// HONESTY. The machine block renders GENERATED wire via lib/exhibitA.ts, which re-adjudicates at
// build time and throws if the shipped package stopped behaving that way. The publication fact
// derives from data/publications.ts — zero literal Zenodo tokens here. The lead's arithmetic is a
// worked scenario shown in full so a reader can check every number.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { citation } from '../../data/publications';
import { CASES, PROVENANCE } from '../../lib/exhibitA';

const theory = citation('w-theory-of-data');

const refusal = CASES.find((c) => c.mood === 'refuse');
if (!refusal) throw new Error('trailhead: the generated transcript carries no refuse case');

// ── THE LEAD'S SCENARIO, AND THE SEMANTIC REPAIR ───────────────────────────────────────────────
// 52 shops on the roster · 3 shut for refurbishment → 49 open · 8 of those had a dead till feed
// → 41 reported · 6 of the REPORTING shops reported an umbrella sale.
//
// THE FIRST CUT WAS WRONG and it is worth writing down why, because the wrong version was more
// comfortable. It offered 6/41, 6/49 and 6/52 as three equally legitimate answers to "what fraction
// of shops sold an umbrella". Only the first is an answer to anything. 6/41 is EXACT — but its
// population is "shops that were reporting", which is not a population anyone means. For the other
// two, six is a KNOWN FLOOR and not the numerator: the eight silent shops did not report zero, they
// reported nothing, and their sales status is unknown. So the honest output for those populations
// is an interval — between 6 and 14 shops — not a number.
//
// The repaired reveal is therefore much better than "all three are legitimate": the visitor believes
// they are choosing a denominator, and discovers they do not possess the numerator they assumed.
// One precise answer to a question nobody asked, and two brackets sixteen points wide.
const KNOWN = 6;
const MAYBE = 14;               // 6 known + up to 8 unknown
const pct = (n: number, d: number) => (100 * n / d).toFixed(1);

const READINGS = [
  {
    k: 'reported',
    d: 41,
    label: 'shops that reported that day',
    exact: true,
    lo: pct(KNOWN, 41),
    hi: pct(KNOWN, 41),
    verdict: 'exact — and about a population nobody means',
  },
  {
    k: 'open',
    d: 49,
    label: 'shops open for business',
    exact: false,
    lo: pct(KNOWN, 49),
    hi: pct(MAYBE, 49),
    verdict: 'somewhere in here. Arithmetic cannot narrow it.',
  },
  {
    k: 'roster',
    d: 52,
    label: 'every shop on the roster',
    exact: false,
    lo: pct(KNOWN, 52),
    hi: pct(MAYBE, 52),
    verdict: 'somewhere in here, and you cannot narrow this one either.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Trailhead — homepage laboratory A"
  description="A laboratory prototype: what if the front page were a few things worth discovering rather than a diagram of the institution?"
  wide={true}
  chip={false}
>

  {/* ── EDGE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  {/* A plain experimental marker, not a masthead. The right-hand slot used to promise "what is worth
      seeing today", which committed us to a cadence; it now says what this actually is. */}
  <header class="edge">
    <p class="edge-l mono">datumwise · homepage laboratory · version A</p>
    <p class="edge-r mono">editorial trailhead</p>
  </header>

  {/* ── 1 · THE LEAD ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="lead" aria-labelledby="lead-h">
    <p class="kicker mono">an ordinary question about umbrellas</p>
    <h1 id="lead-h" class="lead-h">
      Six shops sold an umbrella.<br />What fraction of your shops is that?
    </h1>

    <div class="scene">
      <p class="scene-p">
        A region of <strong>52 shops</strong>, last Tuesday. Three were shut for refurbishment. Of
        the 49 that were open, eight had a dead till feed and sent nothing at all. Of the 41 that did
        report, <strong>six</strong> reported selling an umbrella.
      </p>
      <p class="scene-p scene-ask">
        Nothing above is in dispute. The only thing left to decide is what you divide by.
      </p>
    </div>

    <form class="ballot">
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="visually-hidden">Which shops belong in the denominator?</legend>
        {READINGS.map((r) => (
          <>
            <input class="b-in" type="radio" name="denom" id={`d-${r.k}`} />
            <label class="b-opt" for={`d-${r.k}`}>
              <span class="b-n mono">{r.d}</span>
              <span class="b-t">{r.label}</span>
            </label>
          </>
        ))}

        {/* The reveal. It lives INSIDE the fieldset because `~` only reaches siblings — the first cut
            had it outside and the reveal silently never fired while the picked option still
            highlighted, which is the most convincing kind of broken.
            The argument is carried by SHAPE: one cell holds a number, two hold a bracket. You cannot
            look at the row and think you were choosing between three answers. */}
        <div class="verdict" role="note">
          <p class="v-cap mono">what each choice actually gets you</p>

          <ol class="v-row">
            {READINGS.map((r) => (
              <li class={r.exact ? 'v-cell v-exact' : 'v-cell v-band'} data-k={r.k}>
                <span class="v-mine mono">the one you picked</span>
                {r.exact ? (
                  <span class="v-fig">{r.lo}<span class="v-sign">%</span></span>
                ) : (
                  <span class="v-fig">
                    {r.lo}<span class="v-sign">%</span>
                    <span class="v-dash" aria-hidden="true">–</span>
                    <span class="v-hi">{r.hi}<span class="v-sign">%</span></span>
                  </span>
                )}
                <span class="v-bar" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="v-lab">of {r.label}</span>
                <span class="v-verdict">{r.verdict}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>

          <p class="v-after v-sting">
            You thought you were picking a denominator. Two of those three came back as a bracket,
            because <strong>you do not have the numerator you assumed you had.</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="v-after">
            Six is what the <em>reporting</em> shops reported. The eight silent shops did not report
            zero umbrellas — they reported nothing, and nothing is not a number. Any of them might
            have sold one. So for every population larger than “the shops that were working”, six is
            a floor, and the truth is somewhere in a band sixteen points wide.
          </p>
          <p class="v-after">
            The one exact answer is exact about <em>shops that happened to be reporting</em>, which is
            a population that exists only because a till broke. Nobody has ever wanted to know that.
          </p>
          <p class="v-after v-final">
            Arithmetic will not tell you which of these you are holding. It will happily do the
            division either way, and silence will quietly arrive as a zero.
          </p>

          {/* The serious source, attached to the attraction that earned it — not a shelf. */}
          <div class="source">
            <p class="src-cap mono">the full account of what a population is, and when a number exists</p>
            <a class="src-title" href={theory.href}>{theory.label}</a>
            <span class="src-meta mono">{theory.versionTag ? `${theory.versionTag} · ` : ''}{theory.date} · with proofs</span>
          </div>

          <p class="v-exit">
            Or start one step earlier, at a single number with nothing attached to it at all —
            <a href="/park/when-is-it-data">a four-minute walk</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </fieldset>
    </form>
  </section>

  {/* ── 2 · A SMALL UNRELATED CURIOSITY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  {/* Deliberately about a twentieth the size of the lead, and deliberately about something else
      entirely. This is where the anti-grid defence really lives: an object this small cannot be read
      as one third of a scheme. */}
  <aside class="margin-note" aria-labelledby="mn-h">
    <p class="mn-stamp mono">unrelated, and we keep coming back to it</p>
    <h2 id="mn-h" class="mn-h">Probability: purpose of visit?</h2>
    <p class="mn-p">
      It arrives at the border with the confident air of something that belongs everywhere. Asked to
      state its business, it gives three different answers depending on who is behind the desk: a
      property of the world, a state of somebody's knowledge, or the long-run behaviour of a
      procedure nobody intends to repeat.
    </p>
    <p class="mn-p">
      All three are waved through. They are not the same traveller, they do not license the same
      conclusions, and the number on the passport is identical in every case.
    </p>
    <p class="mn-more">
      <a href="/evidence/walkthrough">The evidence, walked</a> — where this stops being funny.
    </p>
  </aside>

  {/* ── 3 · THE MACHINE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  {/* The one break in the paper ground, and the third KIND of object rather than the third topic.
      It follows the umbrella problem for a reason the page never states out loud: up there,
      arithmetic did the division anyway. Down here, something declines. */}
  <section class="machine ds ds-wire ds-crossing" aria-labelledby="mach-h">
    <div class="mach-in">
      <p class="mach-kick mono">an interruption</p>
      <h2 id="mach-h" class="mach-h">Some questions deserve an answer.</h2>
      <p class="mach-sub">Some don't, and something should be willing to say so out loud.</p>

      <div class="wire">
        <p class="wire-lab mono">asked</p>
        <pre class="wire-req mono">{refusal.request}</pre>

        <p class="wire-lab mono">answered</p>
        <p class="wire-verdict mono">{refusal.mood}</p>

        {refusal.findings.map((f) => (
          <>
            <p class="wire-code mono">{f.code}</p>
            <p class="wire-detail">{f.detail}</p>
          </>
        ))}

        {refusal.noResult && (
          <>
            <p class="wire-lab mono">instead</p>
            <ul class="wire-offers">
              {refusal.noResult.offers.map((o) => <li>{o}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </>
        )}
      </div>

      <p class="mach-prov mono">
        manifold {PROVENANCE.manifold} · columna {PROVENANCE.columna} · contract {PROVENANCE.contract}
        — produced by running the shipped package at build time, not written by hand
      </p>
      <p class="mach-after">
        Refusing is not the software failing. It is the only honest thing left when a question has no
        lawful answer — and it is startlingly hard to buy.
        <a class="mach-more" href="/columna">What this is</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── 4 · THE LIGHT CLOSE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  {/* What is left of the synthesis. It names no architecture, no three questions, and no discipline.
      The bet is that a reader who has met a broken till, a traveller with three stories, and a
      machine that declines will feel the rhyme without being handed it — and that a reader who does
      not feel it would not have been convinced by a diagram either. */}
  <section class="close">
    <hr class="close-rule" />
    <p class="close-line">
      These problems are farther apart than they look. They also rhyme more than they should.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    /* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       VERSION A. Borrows the site's TOKENS and none of its components: the experiment is precisely
       about whether objects may differ, so a shared component costume would decide the question in
       advance. Three objects, three measures, three rhythms, no repeated container.
       ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .mono { font-family: var(--font-mono); }

    /* ── edge ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .edge {
      display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
      width: min(100% - 3rem, 68rem); margin: 2.5rem auto 0; padding-bottom: 0.7rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);
      font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft);
    }
    .edge-r { color: var(--ink); }

    /* ── 1 · the lead ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .lead { width: min(100% - 3rem, 60rem); margin-inline: auto; padding-block: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 5vw, 6rem) 0; }
    .kicker { font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
    .lead-h {
      font-family: var(--font-serif);
      font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 1.2rem + 4.6vw, 4.6rem);
      line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 2.5rem; max-width: 20ch;
    }
    .scene { max-width: 34rem; }
    .scene-p { font-size: 1.06rem; line-height: 1.62; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .scene-ask { color: var(--ink-soft); }

    .ballot { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
    .ballot fieldset { border: 0; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    .b-in { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); white-space: nowrap; }
    .b-opt {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: 5rem minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: baseline; gap: 1.25rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 1.1rem 0; cursor: pointer;
      transition: border-color 0.15s ease;
    }
    .b-opt:last-of-type { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    .b-n { font-size: 1.7rem; color: var(--ink-soft); transition: color 0.15s ease; }
    .b-t { font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.4; }
    .b-opt:hover { border-color: var(--ink); }
    .b-opt:hover .b-n { color: var(--ink); }
    .b-in:checked + .b-opt { border-color: var(--ink); }
    .b-in:checked + .b-opt .b-n { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
    .b-in:focus-visible + .b-opt { outline: 2px solid var(--ds-accent, #7a5c2e); outline-offset: 3px; }

    /* Closed to eyes AND to assistive tech until a commitment is made — clipping alone would let a
       screen reader read the answer out before the question had been answered. */
    .verdict {
      max-height: 0; opacity: 0; overflow: hidden; visibility: hidden;
      transition: max-height 0.5s ease, opacity 0.4s ease;
    }
    .b-in:checked ~ .verdict { max-height: 140rem; opacity: 1; visibility: visible; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
    .v-cap { font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }

    .v-row { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 2.25rem; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 1.75rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .v-cell { display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; align-content: start; border-top: 2px solid var(--rule-strong); padding-top: 0.9rem; }
    .v-mine { font-size: 0.66rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink); visibility: hidden; margin-bottom: 0.1rem; }
    .v-fig { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.05rem + 1.7vw, 2.3rem); line-height: 1.05; }
    .v-sign { font-size: 0.45em; margin-left: 0.08em; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .v-dash { margin: 0 0.18em; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    /* THE ARGUMENT IS THE SHAPE. An exact cell gets a single tick; a bracket gets a span you can see
       is wide. Nobody looking at this row can believe they were choosing between three answers. */
    .v-bar { height: 3px; background: var(--rule-strong); margin: 0.5rem 0 0.35rem; }
    .v-exact .v-bar { width: 3px; background: var(--ink); }
    .v-band .v-bar { width: 100%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--ink) 0 6%, var(--rule-strong) 6% 100%); }
    .v-lab { font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .v-verdict { font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.45; }
    .v-exact .v-verdict { color: var(--ink-soft); }

    #d-reported:checked ~ .verdict .v-cell[data-k='reported'],
    #d-open:checked     ~ .verdict .v-cell[data-k='open'],
    #d-roster:checked   ~ .verdict .v-cell[data-k='roster'] { border-top-color: var(--ink); }
    #d-reported:checked ~ .verdict .v-cell[data-k='reported'] .v-mine,
    #d-open:checked     ~ .verdict .v-cell[data-k='open'] .v-mine,
    #d-roster:checked   ~ .verdict .v-cell[data-k='roster'] .v-mine { visibility: visible; }

    .v-after { max-width: 34rem; font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.62; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
    .v-sting { border-left: 2px solid var(--ink); padding-left: 1rem; }
    .v-final { color: var(--ink-soft); }

    .source { max-width: 34rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 1.1rem; margin-top: 2rem; display: grid; gap: 0.25rem; }
    .src-cap { font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .src-title { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.2rem; }
    .src-meta { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .v-exit { max-width: 34rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }

    /* ── 2 · the small curiosity ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .margin-note {
      width: min(100% - 3rem, 60rem); margin-inline: auto;
      padding-block: clamp(4rem, 3rem + 6vw, 8rem);
      display: grid; justify-items: end;
    }
    .margin-note > * { max-width: 26rem; }
    .mn-stamp { font-size: 0.66rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
    .mn-h { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.35; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .mn-p { font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 0.85rem; }
    .mn-more { font-size: 0.85rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 0; }

    /* ── 3 · the machine ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .machine { background: var(--wire-bg); color: var(--wire-ink); padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 2.5rem + 5vw, 6rem); }
    .mach-in { width: min(100% - 3rem, 46rem); margin-inline: auto; }
    .mach-kick { font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--wire-ink-soft); margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
    .mach-h { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 1.3rem + 2.2vw, 2.8rem); line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
    .mach-sub { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--wire-ink-soft); margin: 0 0 2.5rem; max-width: 32rem; }
    .wire { border-top: 1px solid var(--wire-rule); padding-top: 1.5rem; display: grid; gap: 0.4rem; }
    .wire-lab { font-size: 0.66rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--wire-ink-soft); margin: 1rem 0 0.3rem; }
    .wire-lab:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
    .wire-req { font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0; color: var(--wire-key); background: var(--wire-panel); padding: 0.8rem 1rem; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; }
    .wire-verdict { font-size: 1.5rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 0; color: var(--ds-accent-wire, #c9a86a); }
    .wire-code { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--wire-string); margin: 0.9rem 0 0.25rem; }
    .wire-detail { font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; color: var(--wire-ink); }
    .wire-offers { margin: 0.4rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; }
    .wire-offers li { font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--wire-ink-soft); }
    .mach-prov { font-size: 0.68rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--wire-ink-soft); margin: 2rem 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--wire-rule); padding-top: 0.9rem; }
    .mach-after { font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 1.75rem 0 0; max-width: 32rem; }
    .mach-more { margin-left: 0.5rem; white-space: nowrap; }
    .machine a { color: var(--ds-accent-wire, #c9a86a); }

    /* ── 4 · the light close ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .close { width: min(100% - 3rem, 40rem); margin-inline: auto; padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 2.5rem + 5vw, 7rem); }
    .close-rule { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); margin: 0 0 2rem; }
    .close-line { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1rem + 0.9vw, 1.5rem); line-height: 1.45; margin: 0; }

    /* ── narrow ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    @media (max-width: 46rem) {
      .v-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; }
      .margin-note { justify-items: start; }
      .b-opt { grid-template-columns: 3.5rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0.9rem; }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .verdict { transition: none; } }
  </style>

</BaseLayout>
